  "accuracyNote": "Track centrelines traced from VTA's 15 plan-and-profile sheets (1\" = 40'), found by their 50-ft station ticks, and drawn as the centreline between the two tracks: 2.5 miles as drawn from the conform point with the existing tracks at Wilbur Avenue to the bumping posts beyond Eastridge (VTA: 2.4 miles). Each sheet is fitted to OpenStreetMap streets at the drawing scale (trimmed RMS 0.7-1.7 m), and the sheets are tied together at their match lines and to the middle of the street along Capitol Avenue (where the plans draw the tracks in its median) and Capitol Expressway (where VTA describes the line 'primarily in the median'). As a check, the result lies a median 2 m (90% within 4 m) from OpenStreetMap's own mapping of the tracks under construction, so the line is good to about 5 m, less certain at the Eastridge end. The plans date from the 2018 environmental review; the 2020 and 2021 addenda did not move the tracks, but the final design may differ in detail. Station points are platform middles, not platform outlines. The existing Alum Rock station, north of the plans, is not drawn.",
